      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are touching on a complex area where professionalism intersects with cultural bias. While the *content* (business logic) remains the same, the *connotation* associated with non-standard dialects often leads to a lower initial perception of competence in mainstream corporate settings. This \"filter\" is frequently an inherent bias against varying dialects, rather than a strict measure of intellectual capability. In a diverse modern workplace, organizations are increasingly recognizing the need to value expertise over rigid adherence to a single dialect standard.",
